2025 STATE OF WYOMING 25LSO-0161
HOUSE BILL NO. HB0097
Property conveyances near critical infrastructure.
Sponsored by: Joint Appropriations Committee
A BILL
for
1 AN ACT relating to homeland security; amending duties of
2 county clerks, the division of criminal investigation and
3 the director of the office of homeland security for
4 identification of conveyances near critical infrastructure;
5 repealing requirements to provide a list of designated
6 critical infrastructure zones to the county clerks;
7 amending and creating definitions; and providing for an
8 effective date.
9
10 Be It Enacted by the Legislature of the State of Wyoming:
11
12 Section 1. W.S. 9-1-618(b)(vi), 18-3-402(a)(xxvi),
13 19-13-104(d)(vi), 19-13-501(a)(i), (iv)(A) and by creating
14 a new paragraph (vi) and 19-13-502(c) and (d) are amended
15 to read:
16
1 HB0097

2025 STATE OF WYOMING 25LSO-0161
1 9-1-618. Agents to be safeguarded as peace officers;
2 general assistance to state, county or local authorities;
3 investigative duties.
4
5 (b) The division shall investigate:
6
7 (vi) Conveyances, leases and leasehold interests
8 as defined by 19-13-501(a)(i), within or near designated
9 critical infrastructure zones. as reported by county clerks
10 in accordance with W.S. 19-13-501 and 19-13-502. The
11 division may investigate whether the any conveyance, lease
12 and leasehold interest reported by county clerks in
13 accordance with W.S. 19-13-501 and 19-13-502 may result in
14 a threat to national or state security or whether the
15 conveyance, lease and leasehold interest involves a
16 designated country or person as defined by W.S.
17 19-13-501(a)(iv). The attorney general or, with the
18 attorney general's approval, the division may subpoena
19 witnesses, compel their attendance and require the
20 production of records and other evidence to determine:
21
22 (A) Whether a conveyance, lease and
23 leasehold interest within five (5) miles of a designated
